{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.62,
   "text": "I work the overnight shift at an animal shelter, way out on a county road."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.22,
   "end": 13.465,
   "text": "Forty dogs. And all night long... they never stop barking."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.265,
   "end": 17.551,
   "text": "The woman who trained me gave me one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 18.051,
   "end": 22.424,
   "text": "If the dogs ever go quiet all at once... don't walk the kennels."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 23.124,
   "end": 27.86,
   "text": "Stay in the office. Keep the light on. And wait for them to start again."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 28.66,
   "end": 32.841,
   "text": "For two months, they barked till sunrise. Every single night."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 33.541,
   "end": 39.024,
   "text": "Then, last night, just after three... all forty stopped. At the exact same second."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 40.224,
   "end": 43.509,
   "text": "I sat at my desk... and listened to nothing."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 46.109,
   "end": 50.419,
   "text": "Then, at the far end of the row, the last kennel gate creaked open."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 51.019,
   "end": 55.989,
   "text": "Slow footsteps. Bare feet on wet concrete... coming toward the office."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 56.989,
   "end": 59.315,
   "text": "Then the footsteps stopped."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 61.515,
   "end": 66.357,
   "text": "I looked up at the security monitor... at the camera above my own desk."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 67.157,
   "end": 72.853,
   "text": "Something tall was standing right behind my chair, holding one long finger to its lips."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 74.453,
   "end": 78.613,
   "text": "The dogs hadn't gone quiet on their own... it had asked them to."
  }
 ],
